{"name":"Corydalis Blue","hex":"#a2c7d7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"corydalis","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any member of the genus Corydalis of annual and perennial herbaceous plants in the fumewort family."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corydalis"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Corydalis","blocks":[{"text":"Corydalis is a genus of about 540 species of annual and perennial herbaceous plants in the family Papaveraceae, native to the temperate Northern Hemisphere and the high mountains of tropical eastern Africa. They are most diverse in China and the Himalayas, with at least 357 species in China. Corydalis species are the only dicots having only a single cotyledon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Corydalis_solida_-_Bois_d%27Havr%C3%A9_%281%29.jpg/330px-Corydalis_solida_-_Bois_d%27Havr%C3%A9_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corydalis","wikidata":"Q159568"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Corydalis_ambigua.jpg/120px-Corydalis_ambigua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Corydalis_ambigua.jpg/250px-Corydalis_ambigua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Corydalis_ambigua.jpg/120px-Corydalis_ambigua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACorydalis_ambigua.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Corydalis_aurea_flowers1.jpg/120px-Corydalis_aurea_flowers1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Corydalis_aurea_flowers1.jpg/250px-Corydalis_aurea_flowers1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Corydalis_aurea_flowers1.jpg/120px-Corydalis_aurea_flowers1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACorydalis_aurea_flowers1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Corydalis_buschii_-_%28kiurunkannus%29%2C_%28nunne%C3%B6rt%29%2C_Buschi_l%C3%B5okannus_C_IMG_7699.JPG/120px-Corydalis_buschii_-_%28kiurunkannus%29%2C_%28nunne%C3%B6rt%29%2C_Buschi_